  "narrative": {
    "intro": "North Carolina has received $361M in federal contract obligations so far in FY2027. The state has 5,778 awards to date with an average award size of $62.5K. Obligations fell 93.8% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows larger totals in recent years: FY22 recorded $8.6B, FY23 recorded $7B, FY24 recorded $7.2B, FY25 recorded $9.4B, and FY26 recorded $5.8B, while FY27 stands at $361M. The Department of Agriculture and the Department of Veterans Affairs lead buying activity so far with $118M and $104M respectively. Logging is the largest industry by obligations at $99.6M, and PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the single largest vendor at $99.6M. This snapshot covers partial, fiscal-year-to-date obligations and highlights where spending has concentrated in the state so far in FY2027.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2027 compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 93.8% year over year. Fiscal-year totals before FY27 were much larger: FY26 recorded $5.8B, FY25 recorded $9.4B, FY24 recorded $7.2B, FY23 recorded $7B, and FY22 recorded $8.6B. The FY2027 total so far is $361M, reflecting that current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date. Watch award count and average award size for changes as the fiscal year progresses; current figures are 5,778 awards and $62.5K average award size."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and industries in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $118M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $104M, making them the top two buying agencies. The General Services Administration obligated $37.6M, and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $29.1M. Logging is the top industry at $99.6M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $47.9M and Computer Systems Design Services at $31.5M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the top vendor at $99.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
