      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to North Carolina?",
      "a": "North Carolina received $361M in federal contract obligations so far in FY2027. The state has 5,778 awards with an average award size of $62.5K. Fiscal-year history shows much larger totals in prior years: FY26 recorded $5.8B, FY25 recorded $9.4B, FY24 recorded $7.2B, FY23 recorded $7B, and FY22 recorded $8.6B. Current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date."
